sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant DPMatrix as DPMatrix.run/2
    participant BuildDP as build_dp_matrix/2
    participant ConstructSeq as construct_supersequence/3
    participant Backtrack as backtrack/7

    Client->>DPMatrix: run("Jealous", "Jewel")
    Note over DPMatrix: Entry point for SCS algorithm

    DPMatrix->>BuildDP: build_dp_matrix("Jealous", "Jewel")

    Note over BuildDP: Phase 1: Build LCS DP Array
    BuildDP->>BuildDP: m=7, n=5
    BuildDP->>BuildDP: s1_chars='Jealous', s2_chars='Jewel'
    BuildDP->>BuildDP: arr = :array.new(48, default: 0)  %% (7+1)*(5+1)

    loop Enum.reduce over [{1,1}..{7,5}]
        BuildDP->>BuildDP: char1 = Enum.at(s1_chars, i-1), char2 = Enum.at(s2_chars, j-1)
        alt char1 == char2  (e.g. i=1,j=1: 'J'=='J')
            BuildDP->>BuildDP: get_cell(arr, i-1, j-1, n)  %% :array.get(cell(i-1,j-1,5), arr)
            BuildDP->>BuildDP: new_value = 1 + diagonal_value
        else char1 != char2  (e.g. i=2,j=2: 'e'!='e' → 'e'=='e' match)
            BuildDP->>BuildDP: max(get_cell(arr,i-1,j,n), get_cell(arr,i,j-1,n))
            BuildDP->>BuildDP: new_value = max(top, left)
        end
        BuildDP->>BuildDP: :array.set(cell(i,j,5), new_value, arr)
    end

    Note over BuildDP: arr encodes LCS lengths for all prefixes
    BuildDP-->>DPMatrix: arr (:array, size 48)

    Note over DPMatrix: Phase 2: Construct Supersequence
    DPMatrix->>ConstructSeq: construct_supersequence(arr, "Jealous", "Jewel")
    ConstructSeq->>ConstructSeq: m=7, n=5
    ConstructSeq->>ConstructSeq: s1_chars='Jealous', s2_chars='Jewel'
    ConstructSeq->>Backtrack: backtrack(arr, s1_chars, s2_chars, 7, 5, [], 5)

    Note over Backtrack: Backtrack from (m,n) → (0,0)

    loop Until i=0 and j=0
        alt i=0 (s1 exhausted)
            Backtrack->>Backtrack: prepend s2[j-1], j = j-1
        else j=0 (s2 exhausted)
            Backtrack->>Backtrack: prepend s1[i-1], i = i-1
        else char1 == char2  (shared LCS char)
            Backtrack->>Backtrack: prepend char1, i = i-1, j = j-1
        else get_cell(arr,i-1,j,n) > get_cell(arr,i,j-1,n)
            Backtrack->>Backtrack: prepend s1[i-1], i = i-1
        else
            Backtrack->>Backtrack: prepend s2[j-1], j = j-1
        end
    end

    Backtrack-->>ConstructSeq: acc (charlist, e.g. 'Jeawelous')
    ConstructSeq->>ConstructSeq: List.to_string(acc)
    ConstructSeq-->>DPMatrix: "Jeawelous"

    DPMatrix-->>Client: "Jeawelous"

    Note over Client,Backtrack: Algorithm Complete:<br/>Time: O(m×n), Space: O(m×n)
